 ## Changelog
+- 2026-10-15: Embeddium port (UNVERIFIED: written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain, not compiled, not run; +9 tests not run). New std-only workspace crate `embeddium/` (LGPL-3.0-or-later, `COPYING*` from Embeddium 21.4; no dependencies, so `cargo test -p embeddium` runs on a plain host, which the cdylib cannot): `vis` (`VisibilityEncoding` + the 16^3 flood fill that builds it), `cull` (`OcclusionCuller`: breadth-first walk, a section is entered only through a face pair its neighbour connects; scratch reused, no per-frame allocation), `arena` (`GlBufferArena` allocator: best fit, coalescing, compacting growth capped by `max_buffer_size`), `vertex` (`CompactChunkVertex`, 20 bytes). Wired in: `build_job` computes `Mesh.vis` per section (occluders = `opaque && normal_cube`: leaves, glass, ice, water, slabs, stairs do not hide anything), `ChunkManager::update_visible` runs the walk once per frame (frustum + render shape as the `visible` test, eye outside the world's height = no occlusion, eye chunk not loaded = test every section as before), `draw_ranges(eye, water, draw)` only reads the result. The shadow pass still uses its own frustum. Not wired: the arena and the compact vertex (the terrain `Vertex` is read by `vs_main`, `vs_shadow`, `vs_water` and the G-buffer pass; swapping it means `Vertex::layout` + those entry points, `Unorm16`/`Uint16` attributes decoded in WGSL) and per-region buffers (one draw per chunk run stays; no multi-draw on GLES). Dropped as not applicable: mixins, Forge lighting, the options screen, the GL layer, translucency sorting of faces.
+- 2026-10-15: Radium port (Reforged-Hub/radium-upstream = Lithium for Forge), the three features that exist in b1.7.3 and sit on a hot path (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +3 tests `physics::tests::boxes_agree_with_the_per_cell_scan`, `mobs::tests::explosion_cache_matches_the_plain_ray`, `chunk::phys_tests::meta_only_where_physics_reads_it`, none run). Every change keeps the old answers; the tests compare with the old algorithm.
+    - `entity.collisions.movement` (`LithiumEntityCollisions.getBlockCollisions`): `physics::Boxes` reads the collision boxes of the volume one move can reach once (`step_box`), and `sweep_axis` (3 axes, step-up, 12-step bisections) and the ground test probe that list instead of asking `get` for every cell of the box each time (~2500 lookups per mob step before, ~50 now). A box keeps its cell so a probe counts only the cells `aabb_hits_solid` scanned: same answers, including the 1.5 high fence below the feet that the scan never saw (Java scans one cell lower: UNVERIFIED, left as it was). `debug_assert` fails if a probe leaves the collected volume.
+    - `world.explosions` (`ExplosionMixin.performRayCast`): `Mobs::explode` keeps the cell and its cost between the 0.3 steps of a ray (a cell is entered ~3 times), inserts a cell once; the strength still drops every step and the draws are the same.
+    - `util.chunk_access` idea: `ChunkManager::physics_at` reads the metadata (a 2nd chunk lookup) only for the ids `physics_id` uses (`chunk::meta_matters`); the 3 duplicated lookups in `lib.rs` use it.
