+- 2026-10-15: M22 part 2, boats (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; +4 tests `boat::tests::{floats_settles_and_is_paddled, five_punches_break_it_and_damage_heals, a_hard_slanting_crash_breaks_it_and_others_do_not, boats_push_each_other_and_can_be_picked}`, none run). New `world/boat.rs` = `EntityBoat` (a 1.5 x 0.6 box, Java units: blocks and blocks per 20 Hz tick): buoyancy from 5 slices of its height, paddled by the rider's own walking (`motion += rider.motion * 0.2`, clamped to 0.4 a tick), turns towards where it goes (at most 20 degrees a tick), shoves other boats, wipes snow layers off its path, and a wall hit while it still moves faster than 0.15 a tick along the wall smashes it into 3 planks + 2 sticks (a head-on crash only stops it: `moveEntity` zeroes the motion of the axis that hit, as in b1.7.3). `attackEntityFrom`: damage x 10, over 40 breaks it, the rock decays.
